---
description: Keep the frontend API client in sync with the backend contract
globs: public/**,server.js
alwaysApply: false
---

- The backend contract is `openapi.yaml` in multi-repo-project-b (checked out next to this repo).
- Every call to the backend goes through a method on the client in `public/api.js`.
  The UI in `public/app.js` only uses those methods.
- When you add a client method, check that the endpoint exists in the backend. If it
  does not, add it there in the same task (handler, `openapi.yaml`, and a test).
- Every client method needs a test in `test/api.test.js` that uses the fake `fetchImpl`.
- Build DOM nodes with `document.createElement` and `textContent`, never `innerHTML`
  with API data.
